    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1161">

                <pb facs="0958" n="948" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg948"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.3516/3–2549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Paddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dairen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-25T09:00:00+09:00">March 25, 1949—9
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:22 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. White Russian recently returned from Mukden stated US flag flying over
                    American Consulate General and large house opposite it where all US citizens
                    residing. Guards stationed before both quarters but this also true of Soviet
                    Consulate General (which apparently now exists. See Moscow telegram 4 to
                    Department, repeated Nanking 2<anchor n="35" xml:id="d1161-f1"/>).</p>
                <p>General condition of Mukden “settled down” but some looting and robbery still
                    occurs in outskirts.</p>
                <p>Source says Chinese Communists in complete authority and there little evidence of
                    Soviet political activity.</p>
                <p>Mukden-Dairen trip made by railroad without changing trains at Kwantung
                    border.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 53; repeated Department, Nanking, Shanghai, Shanghai 78, Moscow
                    38.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paddock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1161-f1" n="35" xml:id="d1161-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; in this telegram dated January 2, the Charge in the Soviet Union
                    (Kohler) stated: “Foreign Office note just received states no Soviet Consulate
                    in Mukden present time.” (702.6193/1–249)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
